From 3dec8efb98656ffab3df1bed2dbe8c13e6b93eb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:33:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][GBM] SDR in BT.2020 or DCI-P3 in a split 3D output

SDR of BT.2020 sent as it is (videoscreen.hadessdrbt2020) and HDR mapped
to SDR in a wide gamut (videoscreen.hadessdrhdrgamut) went out in BT.709
in every 3D mode, also in 2D of a 3D video: the composite of the GUI
into SDR of BT.2020 or DCI-P3, which they need, drew into the place of
the left eye only, and the video once with the view off. Since the GUI
is composited over the whole frame and the video is drawn in each eye
(CWholeBuffer, ForEachView() in CApplication::Render()), both go out in
the wide gamut where the eyes are split (side by side, top and bottom,
frame packing), in 2D of a 3D video and without a 3D mode, as a 2D
picture does. Only where Kodi puts both eyes into one picture (anaglyph,
interlaced, checkerboard: KODI::UTILS::STEREO3D::MixesEyes()) they stay
in BT.709, and kodi.log says why.

The defaults (the first setting off, the second at BT.709) change nothing. The help of "HDR
to SDR: gamut of the output" says so (core 62471, Estuary 54471, the
three Spanish ones). Tested: tools/regress/kodi-host stage stereo
(stereo3d_test: SDRWIDE::Check() for every 3D mode, the callers; the
rule before fails). Not tried on a display.
